(7007695, 1059366, 103142, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by tanguera:</b></div><hr/><i> Fabulous, Wendy. You really do have a way with pears. I bet the squirrels are feeling abandoned...<br/> <br/>Can you share your light setup? Looks like two. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Yes -- there was a flash behind the group with one of those 8" velcro soft box attachments (there was also a big window on that side, but I had the speed set to 1/160, so I don''t think that played into it at all), and then I had a shoot through umbrella set up on the right side, close in, pointed at the lone pear. I have no idea what the settings were -- sorry. I''m still trying to learn flash, so I change things a lot. I really love the shoot through umbrella though!! I need to get another one of those. :)</td>', 'Originally posted by tanguera: Fabulous, Wendy. You really do have a way with pears. I bet the squirrels are feeling abandoned... Can you share your light setup? Looks like two.   Yes -- there was a flash behind the group with one of those 8" velcro soft box attachments (there was also a big window on that side, but I had the speed set to 1/160, so I don''t think that played into it at all), and then I had a shoot through umbrella set up on the right side, close in, pointed at the lone pear. I have no idea what the settings were -- sorry. I''m still trying to learn flash, so I change things a lot. I really love the shoot through umbrella though!! I need to get another one of those. :)', '2013-03-27 10:39:42.000000', NULL, 0),
